Z||000000||GT-maniac||05-07-2001||10:51 PM||||My speedomter seems to be permanently stuck all the way over at the far side of the dial. It never seems to move even at startup. Is my speed sensor shot ? Or is it something else ?<BR>On another note, my car will seem to run fine  for a while at idle, idling at around 1200 rpm or so and then will all of sudden starting running really roughly and then just die for no reason I can think of. It usually does this after about five minutes of idling. <BR>Temp and oil pressure seem to be fine, clogged fuel filter maybe ?.<BR>Lastly my car doesn't seem to want to go into  1st, 2nd or reverse, I can get it into these gears if I move the lever at the tranny and I can see the stick moving when I shift it at the transmission so the cable does seem to be intact it just doesn't move the lever at the transmission. Maybe it's stretched ? I had this same problem on my 85 GT with the 4 speed and a new cable seemed to solve the problem. Do I need to do the same thing again ? I hope not, those cables are expensive.<BR>Car is an 87 GT with the 5 speed.<P>Thanks to anyone who replies. ||||reg||9
Z||000001||KRMFiero||05-08-2001||07:32 AM||||Cheack your fuses....  when i bought my 85 the speedo was stuck like around 70 mph and didnt move... then i was looking at my fuses, i replaced a blown one and it started working again!!<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||05-08-2001||08:20 AM||||if the above doesnt work. Remove the lower instrument cluster panel and on the lower left side is a wire bundle that goes into the bottom of the cluster this is the speedo harness just turn on the key and give it a wiggle.||||reg||3
